/*!
\page page_stfgtstrip StFgtStrip

\brief Raw ADC samples, pedestal, and reconstructed charge for one FGT readout strip.

\section fgtstrip_overview Overview

StFgtStrip holds the full per-strip information for the **Forward GEM Tracker (FGT)**.
The FGT has six disc-shaped GEM detectors; each disc/quadrant has two strip layers:
phi-strips (azimuthal coordinate) and r-strips (radial coordinate).  Each strip is
read out by an APV25 chip sampling 15 time bins (~25 ns each).

**Detector**: Forward GEM Tracker (FGT)  
**Stage**: Raw DAQ → pedestal subtraction → charge reconstruction

\section fgtstrip_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StFgtStrip
\endcode

Stored in the FGT strip container (map keyed by geoId) within \c StFgtCollection.

\section fgtstrip_ids Geometry and Electronics IDs

| ID | Description |
|----|-------------|
| \c mGeoId | Geometric strip ID (disc × quadrant × layer × strip); range [0, \c kFgtNumGeoIds) |
| \c mRdo/mArm/mApv/mChan | Electronics coordinates from DAQ (RDO, ARM, APV, channel) |

Strip layer: 'P' = phi-measuring (up to 360/octant), 'R' = radial-measuring (up to 280/octant).

\section fgtstrip_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Int_t | \c mGeoId | Geometric strip ID |
| \c Short_t[15] | \c mAdc | ADC time samples (15 bins, ~25 ns each) |
| \c Short_t | \c mMaxAdc | Maximum ADC across all time bins |
| \c Short_t | \c mClusterSeedType | Cluster seed classification (\c kFgtSeedType*) |
| \c Float_t | \c mCharge | Reconstructed charge (calibration units) |
| \c Float_t | \c mChargeUncert | Charge uncertainty |
| \c Int_t | \c mRdo, \c mArm, \c mApv, \c mChan | Electronics coordinates from DAQ |
| \c Float_t | \c mPed | Pedestal (ADC counts) |
| \c Float_t | \c mPedErr | Pedestal statistical uncertainty |

\section fgtstrip_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c getGeoId() | Geometric strip ID |
| \c getAdc(tb) | ADC at time bin \c tb |
| \c getMaxAdc() | Peak ADC across all time bins |
| \c getCharge() | Reconstructed charge |
| \c getPed() | Pedestal value |
| \c chargeValid() | True if charge is a valid value |
| \c getElecCoords(rdo,arm,apv,chan) | Fill electronics coordinates |

\section fgtstrip_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StFgtStrip* strip = ...; // from FGT strip collection
if (!strip->chargeValid()) continue;
float charge = strip->getCharge();
short maxAdc = strip->getMaxAdc();
for (int tb = 0; tb < kFgtNumTimeBins; ++tb)
    short adc = strip->getAdc(tb);
\endcode

\see StFgtHit, StFgtPoint, StFgtCollection
*/
